    "question": "Write a method named isUnique that takes an array of integers as a parameter and that\nreturns a boolean value indicating whether or not the values in the array are unique (true\nfor yes, false for no). The values in the list are considered unique if there is no\npair of values that are equal.",
    "solution": "public static boolean isUnique(int[] array) {\n    for (int i = 0; i < array.length; i++) {\n        int min = array[i];\n        \n        for (int j = i + 1; j < array.length; j++) {\n            if (min > array[j]) {\n                array[i] = array[j];\n                array[j] = min;\n                min = array[i];\n            }\n        }\n        \n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < array.length - 1; i++) {\n        if (array[i] == array[i + 1]) {\n            return false;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    return true;\n}",
