    "question": "Write a method priceIsRight that accepts an array of integers bids and an integer price\nas parameters. The method returns the element in the bids array that is closest in\nvalue to price without being larger than price.",
    "solution": "public static int priceIsRight(int[] bids, int price) {\n    int difference = 1000000000;\n    int bid = 0;\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < bids.length; i++) {\n        if (bids[i] <= price) {\n            if (price - bids[i] < difference) {\n                bid = bids[i];\n                difference = price - bids[i];\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    if (bid == 0) {\n        return -1;\n    } else {\n        return bid;\n    }\n}",
