    "question": "Write a recursive method indexOf that accepts two Strings as parameters\nand that returns the starting index of the first occurrence of the second\nString inside the first String (or -1 if not found).",
    "solution": "public static int indexOf(String a, String b) {\n    if (a.length() == b.length()) {\n        if (a.equals(b)) {\n            return 0;\n        } \n    } else if (a.length() >= b.length()) {\n        int length = b.length();\n        if (a.substring(0, length).equals(b)) {\n            return 0;\n        } else {\n            int result = 1 + indexOf(a.substring(1), b);\n            if (result != 0) {\n                return result;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return -1;\n}",
