    "question": "Write a method collapse that takes a stack of integers as a parameter\nand that collapses it by replacing each successive pair of integers\nwith the sum of the pair.",
    "solution": "public static void collapse(Stack<Integer> s) {\n    Queue<Integer> q = new LinkedList<Integer>();\n    \n    if (s.size() % 2 != 0) {\n        q.add(s.pop());\n    }\n    \n    while (!s.isEmpty()) {\n        q.add(s.pop() + s.pop());\n    }\n    \n    while (!q.isEmpty()) {\n        s.push(q.remove());\n    }\n    \n    while (!s.isEmpty()) {\n        q.add(s.pop());\n    }\n    \n    while (!q.isEmpty()) {\n        s.push(q.remove());\n    }\n}",
