    "topic": "Linked Lists",
    "question": "Write a method isConsecutive that takes a stack of integers as a parameter and that returns\nwhether or not the stack contains a sequence of consecutive integers starting from the\nbottom of the stack (returning true if it does, returning false if it does not). Consecutive\nintegers are integers that come one after the other, as in 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, etc.",
    "solution": "public static boolean isConsecutive(Stack<Integer> s) {\n    Queue<Integer> q = new LinkedList<Integer>();\n    \n    if (s.size() < 2) {\n        return false;\n    }\n    \n    while (!s.isEmpty()) {\n        q.add(s.pop());\n    }\n    \n    boolean consecutive = true;\n    s.push(q.remove());\n    \n    while (!q.isEmpty()) {\n        if (s.peek() - 1 != q.peek()) {\n            consecutive = false;\n        }\n        s.push(q.remove());\n    }\n    \n    while (!s.isEmpty()) {\n        q.add(s.pop());\n    }\n    \n    while (!q.isEmpty()) {\n        s.push(q.remove());\n    }\n    \n    return consecutive;\n}",
    "hasSourceQuestion": true
