    "topic": "Linked Lists",
    "question": "Write a method shift that takes a stack of integers and an integer n\nas parameters and that shifts n values from the bottom of the stack\nto the top of the stack. You may assume that the parameter n is >= 0\nand not larger than the number of elements in the stack.",
    "solution": "public static void shift(Stack<Integer> s, int n) {\n    Queue<Integer> q = new LinkedList<Integer>();\n    \n    int remove = s.size() - n;\n    \n    while (remove > 0) {\n        q.add(s.pop());\n        remove--;\n    }\n    \n    while (!q.isEmpty()) {\n        s.push(q.remove());\n    }\n    \n    while (!s.isEmpty()) {\n        q.add(s.pop());\n    }\n    \n    while (!q.isEmpty()) {\n        s.push(q.remove());\n    }\n}",
    "hasSourceQuestion": true
