    "question": "Write a method removeRange that accepts a starting and ending index\nas parameters and removes the elements at those indexes (inclusive)\nfrom the list.",
    "solution": "public void removeRange(int startIndex, int endIndex) {\n    if (startIndex < 0 || endIndex < 0) {\n        throw new IllegalArgumentException();\n    } else {\n        int index = 0;\n        ListNode current = front;\n        ListNode start = front;\n        ListNode end = null;\n        \n        while (current != null) {\n        \n            if (index + 1 == startIndex) {\n                start = current;\n            } else if (index == endIndex) {\n                end = current;\n            }\n            \n            current = current.next;\n            index++;\n        }\n        \n        if (startIndex == 0) {\n            front = end.next;\n        } else {\n            start.next = end.next;\n        }\n        \n    }\n}",
