    "question": "Write a method shift that rearranges the elements of a list of integers\nby moving to the end of the list all values that are in odd-numbered\npositions and otherwise preserving list order.",
    "solution": "public void shift() {\n    if (front != null) {\n        int size = 1;\n        ListNode current = front;\n        \n        while (current.next != null) {\n            current = current.next;\n            size++;\n        }\n        \n        ListNode end = current;\n        current = front;\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < size / 2; i++) {\n            end.next = current.next;\n            end = end.next;\n            current.next = current.next.next;\n            current = current.next;\n        }\n        \n        end.next = null;\n    }\n}",
